## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design low-latency, privacy-preserving NLP systems at scale on edge devices. It tests handling of multilingual input with per-tenant isolation, streaming long-form content processing, drift detection across languages, and robust evaluation methodology.

## Key Concepts
- Edge-first inference for sub-200ms chunk latency
- Per-tenant data isolation and logical partitioning
- Privacy budgets using differential privacy (DP) or federated learning (FL)
- Streaming chunked summarization for long-form content
- Cross-language factuality, bias, and drift validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Budget guard for privacy-aware inference
function canInfer(tenantId, inferenceCost, tenantBudgets) {
  const remaining = tenantBudgets[tenantId] ?? 0;
  if (inferenceCost > remaining) {
    throw new Error(`Privacy budget exceeded for tenant ${tenantId}`);
  }
  tenantBudgets[tenantId] = remaining - inferenceCost;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-Up Considerations
When discussing this architecture further, be prepared to address:
- **Model selection**: Lightweight models (T5-small, DistilBERT) for edge deployment vs. larger models for accuracy-critical paths
- **Chunking strategy**: Hierarchical summarization with overlap to preserve cross-sentence context
- **Drift detection**: Monitor BLEU/ROUGE degradation and per-language error rates over time
- **DP implementation**: Noise calibration, privacy budget composition theorems, and epsilon-DP guarantees per tenant
- **Edge orchestration**: Kubernetes at the edge with tenant-aware load balancing and failover

